            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 117,
              "start": 117
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court affirmed that voting discrimination remains a problem in the United States, underscoring the ongoing relevance of the Voting Rights Act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb2b04082193-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 33,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The decision clarifies the standard for evaluating whether voting rules impose racially disparate burdens, affecting future challenges to state election laws."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "eb2b04082193bdd9504dcae829d7cddd88684f276d5a06d69f85691af6d3867e",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-eb2b04082193-0005-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 54,
              "start": 54
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The dissent warns that eliminating pre\u2011clearance review can lead to measurable declines in minority voter turnout, highlighting the protective role of Section\u202f5."
      }
    ],
